	quests: [
		{
			icon: "pirate_hats:pirate_helmet"
			x: 0.0d
			y: -1.75d
			shape: "pentagon"
			subtitle: "Yo ho ho ho!"
			description: [
				"&7Welcome welcome, Bandit. A good fitting name for what we're about to do."
				""
				"&7As the bosses introduced me, I'm ByteSize, or just Byte really. Computer mouse and second in command or whatever job title they gave me."
				""
				"&7Now, you know one way to get that shiny DLC the FOP offer, yeah? Do their tasks, fight their monsters, and send them expensive things for pennies. Or, well, pixels or... Digitized Items as they call them?"
				""
				"&7It's literally a bag of pixels...but I guess it fits! Digital items for a digital currency in a digital world that's just a digital prison for your digitized soul."
				""
				"&7So how about we sail the digital seas and pirate the lot of it, yeah?"
			]
			dependencies: ["14E05D152CF5C051"]
			id: "15363C5FC01E875C"
			tasks: [{
				id: "4A4AE474601F6684"
				type: "checkmark"
				title: "...a Pirate is Free!"
			}]
		}
		{
			title: "The Weak Point"
			icon: "architects_palette:cracked_coal_ore_bricks"
			x: 1.25d
			y: -1.75d
			shape: "pentagon"
			subtitle: "Where to aim the cannon"
			description: [
				"&7So such a large and complex system like the FOP Game Server, its gonna have some weak points. Little bugs, big bugs, bad coding decisions, all sorts of things can weaken a system."
				""
				"&7Especially if you cut corners, try to control too much, don't invest in your security and IT workers, and generally are just a bit dumb in your hiring process, you get BIG weak points."
				""
				"&7The FOP are good at 'reacting' to security breaches, I'll give them that. They closed up the obvious big changes Kowa hit them with early on. But they missed the smaller breaches where we hooked up a conveyor belt to their database."
				""
				"&7That kind of weakness we can exploit. I'll show you, grab a bunch of Glitched Blocks from the Vaults. "
			]
			dependencies: ["15363C5FC01E875C"]
			id: "2EADF7C8D0A49C89"
			tasks: [{
				id: "101AA159D38803FD"
				type: "item"
				title: "5 Glitched Blocks"
				item: {
					id: "itemfilters:tag"
					Count: 1b
					tag: {
						value: "tfb2:glitched_block"
					}
				}
				count: 5L
			}]
			rewards: [{
				id: "16082ACC88CDF7A4"
				type: "choice"
				table_id: 2640422954496342337L
			}]
		}
		{
			title: "A Crack in the Hull"
			icon: {
				id: "create:potato_cannon"
				Count: 1b
				tag: {
					Damage: 0
				}
			}
			x: 2.5d
			y: -1.75d
			shape: "pentagon"
			subtitle: "Shooting The Glowing Spot!"
			description: [
				"&7With so many systems, patches, updates, worlds, and heck even the presence of magic, it all makes nice little weak points we can exploit. But, how do we find them?"
				""
				"&7We need to find Glitches. We at The Ferret Business can use these to bypass the security surrounding their DLC packages. How you ask?"
				""
				"&7As mentioned before, when you are running Vaults, keep an eye out for blocks that are glitching out."
				""
				"&7As well, the bosses should have unlocked the ability to get Glitched items as well. If not, be sure to follow the \"Main Questline\" as well!"
				""
				"&7Be sure to collect all of these you can. "
			]
			dependencies: ["2EADF7C8D0A49C89"]
			id: "2723584BBFD0062D"
			tasks: [{
				id: "0C908F7053658C08"
				type: "checkmark"
			}]
			rewards: [{
				id: "376F5E556E56CE06"
				type: "choice"
				table_id: 2640422954496342337L
			}]
		}
		{
			title: "Greasing the Wheels"
			icon: "minecraft:emerald"
			x: 3.75d
			y: -1.75d
			shape: "pentagon"
			subtitle: "Staff Mistreatment"
			description: [
				"&7Now then, those glitching blocks you got, Bandit, show the little cracks in the system. The little instabilities, the little weak points, call em what you will. "
				""
				"&7They aren't much on their own. Teeny tiny cracks. Most of them can't really be used for anything big."
				""
				"&7But start collecting them, Bandit. And keep collecting them. Each one is like a drop of water: half a dozen of them ain't much, but get a ton of them? Then you got a flood."
				""
				"&7You've probably checked it out, but the Shop Tablet has a variety of items that'll need to spend Glitched stuff on, on top of the Ferret Dollars."
				""
				"&7I'll make sure our systems don't tag glitched blocks with a Value, so you don't accidentally sell them to us."
			]
			dependencies: ["2723584BBFD0062D"]
			id: "4F1D548DFF6D2C28"
			tasks: [{
				id: "35587E84F078AA6E"
				type: "checkmark"
			}]
		}
		{
			title: "The Bigger They Are..."
			icon: "tfb2:glitched_ingot"
			x: 5.0d
			y: -1.75d
			shape: "pentagon"
			subtitle: "...the bigger the weak spots!"
			description: [
				"&7As for the glitched items, the ones you primarily get from the Vault Card system, will be needed for other things in the SHOP Tablet."
				""
				"&7We'll need a combination of both item and block glitches to properly break the system, so tuck all you find away."
				""
				"&7We'll also try to find new ways to find or generate these glitches, so keep your eyes open, Bandit."
			]
			dependencies: ["4F1D548DFF6D2C28"]
			id: "0F59DB9FD98F0E2E"
			tasks: [{
				id: "4722517896F0E07A"
				type: "checkmark"
			}]
		}
		{
			title: "Crime"
			x: 3.75d
			y: -0.5d
			shape: "pentagon"
			subtitle: "or How To Pirate For Blockheads"
			description: [
				"&7Okay, so you know how to find the glitches and things. You've started collecting them. But how are we gonna use them to unlock Research DLC so you don't gotta pay that ridiculous price?"
				""
				"&7We'll have to work with the system security unfortunately, so we can't help unlock ALL of the Research DLC for you... but we can give you a little boost via DLC Bypasses, found in the Shop Tablet."
				""
				"&7Your job? Follow the main questline, find the glitches, and keep pumping in that Audobon Worm. But I do have to warn you, Bandit..."
				""
				"&7A warning : Obtaining a Research DLC Bypass will be very expensive, in Ferret Dollars, in Glitches, and in Tokens."
				""
				"&7Glitches and Tokens are better explained in the main questline, Bandit."
			]
			dependencies: ["0F59DB9FD98F0E2E"]
			id: "29003EE631630364"
			tasks: [{
				id: "493469ABBF3829F5"
				type: "checkmark"
			}]
		}
		{
			icon: {
				id: "minecraft:potion"
				Count: 1b
				tag: {
					Potion: "quark:danger_sight"
				}
			}
			x: 1.25d
			y: -0.5d
			shape: "square"
			subtitle: "or The Rest of the Owl"
			description: [
				"&7Aside from the piratey thing, I'll start up dialogue with the rest of the Researchers here so they can help guide you through the other parts of the FOP Game Server."
				""
				"&7There are lots of mods, with lots of items and machines that the FOP don't really explain to Users. Sure, some have manuals, or guides, but nothing like someone guiding you themselves, yeah? The FOP is more interested in you just sending them the items."
				""
				"&7Now, some of these mods you'll recognize from the previous world, but they may be quite different than you remember. Others will be brand new to you. Either way, the Researchers will start from square one when teaching you."
				""
				"&7And just like before, following the lessons gets you rewards. Money and Blind Boxes. The more we learn, the more we spread the Audobon Worm, the better off we all are."
			]
			dependencies: ["15363C5FC01E875C"]
			id: "132E43CB29BBE90C"
			tasks: [{
				id: "29CE765A6E96998D"
				type: "checkmark"
				title: "The Researchers"
			}]
		}
		{
			icon: "tfb2:ferret_dollar"
			x: 2.5d
			y: -0.5d
			shape: "square"
			subtitle: "Don't Forget the Microtransactions!"
			description: [
				"&7And, of course, we can't forget the extra DLC the FOP have added on top of everything."
				""
				"&7Many mods, especially decoration or building mods, are not gated behind Research or DLC. But most of the big, important ones you'll have to Research to unlock."
				""
				"&7A mod being locked behind Research will usually lock all the recipes behind needing that Research. Not always, some Researched mods have decorative or minor items you can always craft."
				""
				"&7As for the DLC the FOP offer, some of it is unique, but most of it is just... shortcuts. Expensive shortcuts to get resources or gear etc."
				""
				"&7Any of the unique DLC we'll try to offer pirated alternatives for you in the SHOP Tablet."
			]
			dependencies: ["132E43CB29BBE90C"]
			id: "3538C7DDF1408271"
			tasks: [{
				id: "7136D17D2E30849A"
				type: "checkmark"
				title: "Multipass?"
			}]
		}
		{
			title: "The Research Division"
			x: 1.25d
			y: 0.75d
			shape: "gear"
			description: [
				"&7So I'm going to unlock the Research and Development section for you now, Bandit."
				""
				"&7Each quest page here will cover one or more mods. Some Researchers or Research Teams may bundle multiple mods together to cover on a single page."
				""
				"&7I'll more or less have the Q.U.E.S.T. Tablet sort the Research pages alphabetically to the main mod they cover. If it's a Research Group that covers multiple mods, like say both Pam's and Farmer's Delight... um... You'll figure it out! Research Groups will cover similar mods, really."
			]
			dependencies: ["132E43CB29BBE90C"]
